[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661459259","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661459259","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661459259,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eoqU7","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T14:33:25Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T14:35:49Z","body":"Hi!\r\nIf I'm not mistaken, the functionality you're looking for is already available through `filter`:\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar array: Array[int] = [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 10 ]\r\nvar new_array := array.filter(func(v: int): return v % 2 != 0)\r\nprint(array.size() - new_array.size(), \" \", new_array) # Prints 3 [1, 3]\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661459259/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661473465","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661473465","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661473465,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eoty5","user":{"login":"A-Machynak","id":99248176,"node_id":"U_kgDOBepoMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99248176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak","html_url":"https://github.com/A-Machynak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T15:08:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T15:08:04Z","body":"> Hi! If I'm not mistaken, the functionality you're looking for is already available through `filter`:\r\n> \r\n> ```gdscript\r\n> var array: Array[int] = [ 0, 1, 2, 3, 10 ]\r\n> var new_array := array.filter(func(v: int): return v % 2 != 0)\r\n> print(array.size() - new_array.size(), \" \", new_array) # Prints 3 [1, 3]\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nYes, but this unfortunately creates a new array. Creating a new one every time I (**might**) want to delete something doesn't sit well with me. For my use case, I'd call this method often, but usually it wouldn't delete anything.\r\n\r\nThough if this is the idiomatic \"godot way\" to do this, so be it. I just thought that a method similar to the erase-remove idiom is missing from the API and someone else might feel the same way.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661473465/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661478451","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661478451","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661478451,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eovAz","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T15:19:24Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T15:19:24Z","body":"> For my use case, I'd call this method often, but usually it wouldn't delete anything.\r\n\r\n`filter` is certainly a lot slower than an in-place `filter`, `retain` or `erase_custom`. Often, this wouldn't matter, but for some use-cases, it does. GDScript's mentality of \"duplicate for changes\" is convenient, but has this problem for a lot of functions.\r\n\r\nFor your use-case specifically, `Array::filter` could (and should!) be optimized _not_ to create a new `Vector` instance when no arrays were filtered. Instead, in this case it could create a shallow CoW copy. In cases where no items are modified, this should be just as fast as in-place modifications.\r\n\r\nI'll make a note of optimizing the function for that :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661478451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661480955","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661480955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661480955,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eovn7","user":{"login":"A-Machynak","id":99248176,"node_id":"U_kgDOBepoMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99248176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak","html_url":"https://github.com/A-Machynak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T15:25:22Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T15:25:22Z","body":"> For your use-case specifically, `Array::filter` could (and should!) be optimized _not_ to create a new `Vector` instance when no arrays were filtered.\r\n\r\nThat's another way to do it I guess. For me, it just doesn't seem right to add some overhead where it obviously isn't needed, ergo my solution. I guess I'll stick to my solution in the meantime. You can close this PR if you feel like it isn't useful.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661480955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661511477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661511477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661511477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eo3E1","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T16:27:54Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T17:35:14Z","body":"I implemented my proposed solution: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102919\r\n\r\nI observed only 5% speed up, even for the optimized case. This means that other parts of the loop (e.g. call frames through `callp`) are a more important bottleneck than `Array` reallocation.\r\n\r\nThis is important info for this PR as well: It may be possible that your reverse array loop you threw in as a workaround above is actually faster than your `erase_custom` implementation (though I didn't test this). The reason being the same as in my own PR.\r\n\r\nAll in all, I think it would be much more important / helpful for your case to optimize `GDScript` VM calls, especially on minimal lambda functions. Neither my nor your proposed speed up is unlikely to make your own use-case that much faster without that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661511477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661533899","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102915#issuecomment-2661533899","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102915","id":2661533899,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6eo8jL","user":{"login":"A-Machynak","id":99248176,"node_id":"U_kgDOBepoMA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99248176?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak","html_url":"https://github.com/A-Machynak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/A-Machynak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-16T17:22:03Z","updated_at":"2025-02-16T17:22:03Z","body":"> I implemented my proposed solution: #102919\r\n\r\nThank you very much for that. You're completely right and I blame the terrible benchmarks I wrote. The workaround I mentioned is basically twice as fast, which is kinda unfortunate. I don't gain much from not using the filter either. I guess that I'll have to look more into the VM code. Thanks for your time - closing this.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2661533899/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]